# Catalog data

- `brands.name` is unique after lowercase, NFD diacritic removal, non-alphanumeric removal, and trim.
- Store canonical spelling (`Citroën`, `Škoda`, `MINI`), never ASCII/case duplicates (`Citroen`, `Skoda`, `Mini`).
- `vehicle_models` belongs to one brand through `brand_id`; `vehicleType` is `car`, `truck`, or `moto`.

## Slugs

- Use `createSlug`, `slugMatches`, and fallback-only `slugToName` from the shared slug utilities; do not reimplement them.
- URLs omit diacritics (`citroen/c-elysee`); titles use database names (`Citroën C-Elysée`).
- Resolve by `createSlug(name) === slug` before legacy lowercase-name fallback.

## Data changes

- Keep corresponding brand/model data synchronized in `core/backend/src/scripts/stage/` and `production/`.
- Use `fix-brand-duplicates.ts` for canonical duplicate cleanup.
- After database changes run `cd core/backend && npm run clear-cache:brands`.
- Invalidate `brands:*`, `brands:models:*`, and `listings:search:*`.
